    {
      "id": "authoring-sql-p3",
      "title": "Subqueries and missing matches",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "authoring-sql-p3-title",
          "type": "text",
          "role": "title",
          "text": "Subqueries and missing matches",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 38,
            "minFontSize": 32,
            "overflow": "error"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "authoring-sql-p3-b1",
          "type": "text",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 22,
            "minFontSize": 20,
            "lineHeight": 1.3,
            "overflow": "error"
          },
          "text": "Scalar and correlated subqueries\nA scalar subquery supplies one value. NOT EXISTS keeps rows with no matching child; it also avoids NOT IN surprises caused by NULL."
        },
        {
          "id": "authoring-sql-p3-b2",
          "type": "code",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 22,
            "minFontSize": 20,
            "lineHeight": 1.3,
            "overflow": "error"
          },
          "language": "sql",
          "title": "Above-average orders",
          "code": "SELECT id FROM orders\nWHERE amount > (SELECT AVG(amount) FROM orders)\nORDER BY amount DESC, id;"
        },
        {
          "id": "authoring-sql-p3-b3",
          "type": "code",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 22,
            "minFontSize": 20,
            "lineHeight": 1.3,
            "overflow": "error"
          },
          "language": "sql",
          "title": "Customers without orders",
          "code": "SELECT id FROM customers AS c\nWHERE NOT EXISTS (\n  SELECT 1 FROM orders AS o\n  WHERE o.customer_id = c.id\n)\nORDER BY id;"
        },
        {
          "id": "authoring-sql-p3-b4",
          "type": "table",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 22,
            "minFontSize": 20,
            "lineHeight": 1.3,
            "overflow": "error"
          },
          "columns": [
            "pattern",
            "result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Above-average orders",
              "id = 2"
            ],
            [
              "Customers without orders",
              "id = Cy"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "authoring-sql-p3-b5",
          "type": "text",
          "style": {
            "fontSize": 22,
            "minFontSize": 20,
            "lineHeight": 1.3,
            "overflow": "error"
          },
          "text": "Practice: preserve input grain\nAdd an order with a NULL customer_id and compare NOT IN with NOT EXISTS. Add a second order at the same timestamp and explain the tie-breaker on page 2."
        }
      ],
